#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:795
msgid "Keyboard shortcut to show the primary menu"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:809
msgid "Whether shortcuts are enabled"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:810
msgid ""
"Whether shortcuts are enabled. They may interfere with some applications run "
"inside the terminal so it’s possible to turn them off."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:819
msgid "Whether the standard GTK shortcut for menubar access is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:820
msgid ""
"Normally you can access the menubar with F10. This can also be customized "
"via gtkrc (gtk-menu-bar-accel = \"whatever\"). This option allows the "
"standard menubar accelerator to be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:830
msgid "Whether the shell integration is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:831
msgid ""
"This is about GNOME Shell: whether terminals can be found in its search. See "
"inject-shell-integration for the integration of the shells in the terminals."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:836
msgid "Whether to add shell integration to bash, zsh and fish"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:837
msgid ""
"If true, the default shell of a profile is started so that it reports its "
"prompts, commands and working directory, which command notifications, prompt "
"navigation and copying command output need. Custom commands, login bash "
"shells and terminals in containers are left alone."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:842
msgid "Whether to ask for confirmation before closing a terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:847
msgid "Additional info section items to appear in the context menu"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:852
msgid "Whether to open new terminals as windows or tabs"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:857
msgid "When to show the tabs bar"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:863
msgid "Width of the tab list when the tabs are on the left or right"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:867
msgid "The position of the tabs bar"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:872
msgid "Which theme variant to use"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:877
msgid ""
"Whether new tabs should open next to the current one or at the last position"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:882
msgid "What a middle click on a tab does"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:883
msgid ""
"“close” closes the tab; “paste” switches to the tab and pastes the primary "
"selection into it."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:888
msgid "Whether windows should have rounded corners"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:893
msgid "The space between the terminal text and the edges of the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:894
msgid ""
"“none” removes it, also next to rounded window corners; “small” keeps the "
"text clear of rounded corners; “large” leaves more room."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:901
msgid ""
"Whether the user has been asked to import the settings of GNOME Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:906
msgid ""
"Whether to give the header bar and the tabs the colors of the active terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:907
msgid ""
"Only when the terminal uses a color scheme or colors of its own, not the "
"system style; the colors for root and remote sessions take precedence."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:912
msgid "Whether to dim the panes of a split tab other than the active one"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:917
msgid "Whether to show a title bar above each pane of a split tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:922
msgid "Regular expressions for more text that quick select offers"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:923
msgid ""
"Quick select labels URLs, paths, hashes, addresses and numbers; matches of "
"these Perl-compatible regular expressions are offered too, before those."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:928
msgid "Whether to ignore the titles that programs set"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:929
msgid ""
"If true, terminals show the title set with “Set Title…” or the --title "
"option, or else their working directory, instead of the title that programs "
"set with escape sequences."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:934
msgid "Whether to show a short notice after copying to the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:939
msgid ""
"Whether to notify when a long-running command finishes in the background"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:940
msgid ""
"Needs a shell that reports its commands, for example bash or zsh with the "
"VTE shell integration (vte.sh)."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:946
msgid "How long a command must run, in seconds, before its end is notified"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:952
msgid ""
"How long, in seconds, a terminal monitored for silence must be quiet before "
"that is notified"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:958
msgid "Width of the quick terminal, in percent of the screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:964
msgid "Height of the quick terminal, in percent of the screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:969
msgid ""
"Whether the quick terminal hides when another application gets the focus"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:974
msgid "Whether the quick terminal slides in from the top edge of the screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:975
msgid "Only on X11, where applications can place their windows."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:980
msgid ""
"Whether to ask the desktop for a system-wide shortcut for the quick terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:981
msgid ""
"Uses the GlobalShortcuts portal (GNOME 48 or newer, KDE Plasma). The desktop "
"sends the shortcut only to a running application, so Pano Terminal then "
"keeps running in the background and starts when you log in."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:986
msgid "Whether to show when a terminal runs as root or over SSH"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:987
msgid ""
"Colors the header bar and marks the tab while the foreground program of the "
"terminal runs as root (for example sudo or su) or connects to another "
"computer (ssh, mosh)."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:992
msgid ""
"Whether new tabs and panes start in the container of the terminal they are "
"opened from"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:993
msgid ""
"Works for Toolbox and Distrobox containers. The shell inside the container "
"has to report it (Toolbox does), or the terminal has to be started in it "
"from Pano Terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:998
msgid ""
"Whether to reopen the windows, tabs and panes of the last session on startup"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:999
msgid ""
"Applies when Pano Terminal is started without arguments and no window is "
"open. Each terminal gets a new shell in its previous working directory; "
"running programs are not restored."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:1004
msgid "Whether programs may resize the window"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:1005
msgid ""
"If true, a program in the active terminal can resize the window with an "
"escape sequence, as the resize command does. Terminals in other tabs and "
"panes of a split tab never can."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:1009
msgid "Whether new windows get the size of the last used terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:1010
msgid ""
"When enabled, new windows use the number of columns and rows of the terminal "
"used last, instead of the initial size of the profile."
msgstr ""

#: src/com.aripd.Pano.gschema.xml:1015
msgid "Always check whether Pano Terminal is the default terminal"
msgstr ""

